        <headline>Special Weather Statement issued September 24 at 9:49AM EDT by NWS Wilmington NC</headline>
        <description>At 949 AM EDT, the public reported a strong thunderstorm near
Nixonville, or 9 miles east of Conway, moving northwest at 5 mph.

HAZARD...Wind gusts up to 40 mph and pea size hail.

SOURCE...Public.

IMPACT...Gusty winds could knock down tree limbs and blow around
unsecured objects. Minor hail damage to vegetation is
possible.

Locations impacted include...
Conway, Horry, Loris, Hickory Grove, Homewood, Hammond, Adrian,
Bayboro, Hand, Allsbrook, Nixonville, and Loris Community Hospital.
</description>
        <instruction>If outdoors, consider seeking shelter inside a building.</instruction>
